/target

# No lock. Every day crate is a bare git dependency on main, and this repository's job is to prove
# itself against the newest one: CI resolves a fresh lock on every run, and a committed one would
# only pin staleness — or, after `day patch --local`, record the paths of one developer's machine.
# A superapp that depends on this crate commits its own lock.
/Cargo.lock

# Machine-local: `day patch --local <checkout>` writes this to build against a day checkout instead
# of the git dependency. CI has no such file and resolves git.
/.cargo/config.toml
